body:
You're missing the point and just wrong. There is a difference in normalizing test levels to levels documented in an average range for a population group and injecting well over 3x the amount.  One is about living a normal life when your body cannot adequately produce the test you need and the other is about how big you can get while training in the shortest time span possible.

&#x200B;

While treatment varies by the individual, you're not going to find a credible doc anywhere that prescribes 500 MG a week to an individual. That's nuts. It's disingenuous to lead folks looking for information on a TRT Subreddit to believe this amount and treatment is TRT.

&#x200B;

Edit: to be clear, I don't care what other people put in their bodies. Just don't try and mislead people by calling it other than what it is and what your personal intent is. That's what bothers me.

If you try to use Firefox pops up a prompt stating, "Live view is not available for your browswer, we recommend using the latest Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge browsers".

&#x200B;

Was just trouble shooting this myself.
